    {
      "id": "33fc6b7133bc44f134bf9ddd40350aee318518ce",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2007465574,
          "type": null,
          "body": "ENC_NA is just a 0, so xoring with 0 is basically a NOP anyhow. So I guess this should work.\n\nWhat I do not understand:\n- What are you fixing?\n- Why only change left side and not right side too?",
          "author": {
            "id": 6878858,
            "username": "LarsVoelker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Dr. Lars Völker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/cccf2084a0438673e9e09f07ed0a5035f6e8815d3d5d888db0023a757c8dce8c?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/LarsVoelker"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-07-19T09:11:53.338Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-07-19T09:11:53.338Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 316222520,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 16497,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "f7fce8eee2ca4a58051f952062ad57ac8f76c4f7",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2007477391,
          "type": null,
          "body": "On the l.h.s, if we want to match cases where we assigned ENC_ASCII | ENC_NA (i.e. line 2993), it won't.  We are ORing (|), not XORing (^)\n\nOn the r.h.s, ENC_UTF_8 is 2, so it can be usefully ORed with.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Martin Mathieson",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/030414c33f619ee28811cd9c073802ef2267d160ab2744eb8427bd49af4c7998?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/martin.r.mathieson"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-07-19T09:18:50.490Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-07-19T09:20:50.112Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 316222520,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 16497,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "6bb57c7985b9b1b9b92c5f85650b9de55c3ac7a8",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2007498516,
          "type": null,
          "body": "To be clear, you cannot treat ENC_ASCII (0) as a mask, and check using & that it is set in str_encoding.\n\nIt looks as though the test is supposed to catch the cases from lines 2989 (UTF8) and 2993 (ASCII), but as it is, won't match with the ASCII case.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Martin Mathieson",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/030414c33f619ee28811cd9c073802ef2267d160ab2744eb8427bd49af4c7998?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/martin.r.mathieson"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-07-19T09:30:27.189Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-07-19T09:30:43.953Z",
